<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>API Home Page</title>
   <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.png">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/footer.css">
</head>

<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Welcome to the API Home Page</h1>
        <p>Use the following routes to interact with the API using Postman or any other API tool:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>GET /users</strong> - <a href="<%= APP_URI %>/users">Fetch all users</a></li>
            <li><strong>GET /users/:student_id</strong> - <a href="<%= APP_URI %>/users/50">Fetch a user
                    by ID</a></li>
            <li><strong>GET /api/users</strong> - Fetch all users (API)</li>
            <li><strong>POST /api/users</strong> - Create a new user (API)</li>
            <li><strong>GET /api/users/:student_id</strong> - Fetch a user by ID (API)</li>
            <li><strong>PATCH /api/users/:student_id</strong> - Update a user by ID (API)</li>
            <li><strong>DELETE /api/users/:student_id</strong> - Delete a user by ID (API)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Replace <code>:student_id</code> with the actual student ID when testing the routes.</p>

        <h2>POST /users and POST /api/users</h2>
        <p>To create a new user, send a POST request make sure you use the following JSON body:</p>
        <pre>
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyToClipboard('postJson')">Copy</button>
            <code id="postJson">
{
  "first_name": "whatever you want ",
  "last_name": "whatvere u want ",
  "email": "give differnt mail every time ",
  "age": whatever you give in integer ,
  "major": "whatever subject u can give ",
  "gpa": whatever u number can give ,
  "enrollment_date": "in format YYYY/MM/DD",
  "graduation_date": "in format YYYY/MM/DD"
}
            </code>
        </pre>

        <h2>PATCH /users/:student_id and PATCH /api/users/:student_id</h2>
        <p>To update a user, send a PATCH request with the JSON body containing only the fields you want to update. For
            example, to update the email and age:</p>
        <pre>
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyToClipboard('patchJson')">Copy</button>
            <code id="patchJson">
{
  "email": "new.email@example.com",
  "age": 22
}
            </code>
        </pre>
        <p>Note: In the PATCH method, you do not need to send the whole schema, only the data which needs to be updated.
        </p>
    </div>

    <%- include('footer') %>
    <script src="/scripts/index.js"></script>
    <script src="/scripts/footer.js"></script>

</body>
</html>